-- Rewrites the stored key of the 22 encyclopedia sources the vocabulary seed now cites as entries in the print work, with its editor,
-- edition, place, publisher and year, to the citation `citationText` renders for each today. It does the same for de Groot's
-- Religious System of China volumes IV and VI in `compendium/sources/`, whose files gained a place, a publisher and the title page's
-- wording in the note. A reference's `seed_key` is that rendered text and the seed finds a source by it alone, so without this the
-- seed would read each stored row as missing and insert a second copy.
-- With it, the row keeps its id and its links, and the next seed run writes the new fields onto it unless a person has edited it.
-- Each pair names one source's old key and its new one. Only a compendium row is touched (a coven's own source has no seed row to
-- find); a soft-deleted row is rewritten too, so the seed still reads that source as deleted and does not bring it back. Where any
-- compendium row already holds the new key, the old row is left as it is, as the unique index allows one live row per key and the seed
-- reads a key held twice as either row. `updated_by` is left as it was, so a person's edit still reads as theirs to the seed.
-- A SQL migration cannot revalidate the unstable_cache "compendium" tag; the deploy that runs it starts a fresh cache.
UPDATE "references" r SET "seed_key" = p."new_key"
FROM (VALUES
  ('"Lilith." In Encyclopaedia Judaica. 2nd ed. 2007. Jewish Virtual Library. Accessed October 6, 2026. https://www.jewishvirtuallibrary.org/lilith.', 'Encyclopaedia Judaica, 2nd ed., under "Lilith." Edited by Fred Skolnik and Michael Berenbaum. Detroit: Macmillan Reference USA in association with the Keter Publishing House, 2007. Jewish Virtual Library. Accessed October 6, 2026. https://www.jewishvirtuallibrary.org/lilith. (Print details from the Library of Congress catalogue record, LCCN 2006020426.)'),
  ('Pope, Marvin H. "Anath." In Encyclopaedia Judaica. Encyclopedia.com. Accessed October 6, 2026. https://www.encyclopedia.com/people/philosophy-and-religion/biblical-proper-names-biographies/anath.', 'Pope, Marvin H. Encyclopaedia Judaica, 2nd ed., under "Anath." Edited by Fred Skolnik and Michael Berenbaum. Detroit: Macmillan Reference USA in association with the Keter Publishing House, 2007. Encyclopedia.com. Accessed October 6, 2026. https://www.encyclopedia.com/people/philosophy-and-religion/biblical-proper-names-biographies/anath. (Print details from the Library of Congress catalogue record, LCCN 2006020426.)'),
  ('Gimbutas, Marija. "Slavic Religion." In Encyclopedia of Religion. Encyclopedia.com. Accessed October 6, 2026. https://www.encyclopedia.com/environment/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/slavic-religion.', 'Gimbutas, Marija. Encyclopedia of Religion, 2nd ed., under "Slavic Religion." Edited by Lindsay Jones. Detroit: Macmillan Reference USA, 2005. Encyclopedia.com. Accessed October 6, 2026. https://www.encyclopedia.com/environment/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/slavic-religion. (Print details from the Library of Congress catalogue record, LCCN 2004017052.)'),
